# DTF tier manifest: device-auth-flow  (artifact-keeper#3549, closes #3461)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + auth.device (DEVICE_AUTH_ENABLED=true,
# poll interval 2 s, device-code request limit raised to 100 per window).
#
# THE FEATURE (#3461, shipped by #3549 as 5fb190bd, migration 292, 1.12.0)
# The OAuth 2.0 Device Authorization Grant (RFC 8628) as a plain AK grant:
#   POST /api/v1/auth/device/code   (no auth)  -> device_code, user_code,
#                                                 verification_uri, interval,
#                                                 expires_in
#   POST /api/v1/auth/device/token  (no auth)  -> authorization_pending /
#                                                 slow_down / access_denied /
#                                                 invalid_grant, then ONE token
#   POST /api/v1/auth/device/{verify,approve,deny}  (interactive session JWT)
#   GET  /device                                (the approval page)
# Off unless DEVICE_AUTH_ENABLED=true; while off every route answers 404.
# Security model asserted here (read from api/handlers/device.rs and
# services/device_service.rs, not the PR body):
#   * `*` and `admin` are never grantable: /code answers 400 invalid_scope;
#     a non-admin approver's admin-only scopes (delete:artifacts ...) are
#     withheld, and a request of only those is refused at approve (403).
#   * the token is minted for the APPROVING user at the granted scopes.
#   * single use: a second redemption is invalid_grant + DEVICE_TOKEN_REJECTED
#     (reason replay).
#   * failed-code budget (5 per user per 900 s, shipped default) reserved
#     BEFORE the code lookup: once spent, even the correct code answers 429.
#   * only an interactive session may approve: API tokens, Basic, device-
#     issued (scoped) tokens and a locked account are refused (403, audited).
#   * signing out the approving session after approval voids it: the next
#     poll is invalid_grant + DEVICE_TOKEN_REJECTED (approver_sessions_revoked).
#   * codes are stored as SHA-256 digests only; audit rows for every step.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      the flow and every refusal above. RED on 1.11.3, where no
#              device route exists.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images: local login + /auth/me, API-token use;
#              and, after the oracle recreates the backend on the SAME compose
#              project with DEVICE_AUTH_ENABLED=false, every device route
#              answers 404 to an authenticated caller and login still works.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~60 calls back to back from one IP. The device
# failed-code throttle under test ignores RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED by design.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem auth.device"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
